<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Selymbria</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Silivri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Selymbria was an ancient Greek city on the northern shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-marmara">Sea of Marmara</a>, founded by colonists from Megara in the seventh century BCE, and like its neighbour <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> it guarded the sea route to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>. It was a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delian-league">Delian League</a> in the fifth century BCE. It survives as the town of Silivri in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istanbul">Istanbul</a> Province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>.</p></div>
